---
title: Upload from Path
description: Upload files from local filesystem or browser to Pinnacle cloud storage
---

Uploads a file to Pinnacle's cloud storage. The method handles file validation, MIME type detection, and manages the complete upload process including pre-signed URL generation.

## Parameters

<Tabs>
  <Tab title="TypeScript" language="typescript">
    | Parameter | Type | Description |
    |-----------|------|-------------|
    | `fileInput` | `string \| File` | File path string (Node.js) or File object (browser) |
    | `options` | `object` (optional) | Upload configuration |
    | &nbsp;&nbsp;`name` | `string` | Display name (defaults to file basename or File.name) |
    | &nbsp;&nbsp;`options` | [`UploadFileParams.Options`](/api-reference/tools/upload-file#request.body.options) | Additional file options (e.g., download settings) |
  </Tab>

<Tab title="Python" language="python">
  | Parameter | Type | Description | |-----------|------|-------------| |
  `file_path` | `str` | Absolute or relative path to the file to upload | |
  `name` | `str` (optional) | Display name (defaults to file basename) | |
  `options` |
  [`UploadFileOptions`](/api-reference/tools/upload-file#request.body.options) |
  Additional file options (e.g., download settings) |
</Tab>

  <Tab title="Ruby" language="ruby">
    Coming soon
  </Tab>
</Tabs>

## Returns

Returns the download URL as a string.

## Errors

| Error                 | Description                                                                                  |
| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `NotFoundError`       | File does not exist at the specified path (Node.js only)                                     |
| `BadRequestError`     | Path points to a directory instead of a file, or invalid file input type for the environment |
| `InternalServerError` | File system operation failed (permissions, disk errors)                                      |

## Example Implementation

<Tabs>
  <Tab title="TypeScript" language="typescript">
    ### Node.js

    ```typescript
    import { PinnacleClient } from 'rcs-js';

    const client = new PinnacleClient({ apiKey: process.env.PINNACLE_API_KEY });

    // Upload from file path
    async function uploadDocument() {
      try {
        // Returns the download URL as a string
        const downloadUrl = await client.tools.file.uploadFromPath(
          './media/video.mp4',
          {
            name: 'Product Demo Video',
            options: {
              download: {
                expiresAt: '2025-12-31T23:59:59Z'
              }
            }
          }
        );

        console.log('Download URL:', downloadUrl);
        return downloadUrl;
      } catch (error) {
        throw error;
      }
    }
    ```

    ### Browser

    ```typescript
    import { PinnacleClient } from 'rcs-js';

    const client = new PinnacleClient({ apiKey: process.env.PINNACLE_API_KEY });

    // Upload from File object (e.g., from file input)
    async function uploadFromInput(file: File) {
      try {
        const downloadUrl = await client.tools.file.uploadFromPath(
          file,
          {
            name: 'User Upload',
            options: {
              download: {
                expiresAt: '2025-12-31T23:59:59Z'
              }
            }
          }
        );

        console.log('Download URL:', downloadUrl);
        return downloadUrl;
      } catch (error) {
        throw error;
      }
    }

    // Example with file input element
    document.getElementById('fileInput')?.addEventListener('change', async (e) => {
      const file = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).files?.[0];
      if (file) {
        await uploadFromInput(file);
      }
    });
    ```

  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Python" language="python">
    ```python
    from rcs import AsyncPinnacle
    import os

    client = AsyncPinnacle(api_key=os.environ.get("PINNACLE_API_KEY"))

    # Upload from file path
    async def upload_document():
        try:
            # Returns the download URL as a string
            download_url = await client.tools.file.upload_from_path(
                './media/video.mp4',
                name='Product Demo Video',
                options={
                    'download': {
                        'expires_at': '2025-12-31T23:59:59Z'
                    }
                }
            )

            # download_url is a string
            print('Download URL:', download_url)
            return download_url
        except Exception as error:
            raise error
    ```

  </Tab>

